r estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 27     SPECIAL STAINS Addendum     THE CARCINOMA CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR CHROMOGRANIN WITH IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINING    Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number are three parts  Labeled  left breast mass  is a 18 gram fragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm with overlying skin ellipse REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm with central healing scar 2 0cm in length  There is a long suture at one end of the specimen and a short suture at a side of the specimen  the long suture is designated 12 o clock  and the short suture designated 9 o clock  The external surface of the specimen is unremarkable  lobulated  yellow pink fibroadipose tissue with focal cautery artifact and fibrous tissue  The external surface is inked black with the 9 o clock aspect inked yellow on black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a central biopsy cavity REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm surrounded by gritt