m    has a well healed scar  1 9cm in length   The specimen is inked by the  surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior    black  anterior   blue  superior   red  inferior   green  lateral   yellow   medial   orange  Two  2 cm deep to the scar there is an area consistent with  biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  This area is adjacent to the  medial margin and the superior margin  The area is 3cm from the inferior  margin  3 5cm from the lateral margin  2cm from the anterior margin  skin   and 3 2cm from the posterior margin  Representative sections are submitted  for histologic evaluation   Micro 3  skin to biopsy cavity  anterior margin   3 frags  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  entire biopsy cavity with closest margin  superior and medial   10  frags  ESS   Micro 10  additional superior and medial margins  2 frags  RSS   Micro 11  additional anterior margin  2 frags  RSS   Micro 12  posterior margin  2 frags  RSS   Micro 13  inferior margin  2 frags  RSS   Micro 14  lateral margin  2 frags  RSS   NOTE  The specimen is approximately 70  fat and 30  fibrous tissue  All  fibrous tissue has been submitted   mir  Reports to  KAELIN  CAROLYN  MARY M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST MASTECTOMY   PARTIAL OR SIMPLE   report_end  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 10 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 3 OF 3  EXTENDING TO AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  WITH METASTASIS TO AN INTRA PARENCHYMAL LYMPH NODE  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  In situ carcinoma is not identified  Estrogen and progesterone receptor status will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm nodule of breast tissue with a well demarcated  irregular firm and gritty white to gray nodule  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm in size abutting an inked resection margin  A portion of the suspicious nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  submitted entirely in A through I  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Absent.
