Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  John H Eichhorn  M D  Reports To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Tissue Processed CLINICAL DATA  Left breast carcinoma  with positive margins on prior excision  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING NUMEROUS CALCIFICATIONS  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE OR IN SITU CARCINOMA  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision  long  lateral  short  superior   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm portion of tan red fibrofatty breast tissue with a short black stitch designating the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margin  An exposed REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hemorrhagic cavity consistent with a previous biopsy site is along the anterior aspect  The cavity has been previously and partially stitched together with black sutures  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the medial green  and the lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a focal bright yellow area consistent with fat necrosis surrounding the hemorrhagic cavity  The cavity focally abuts the medial margin  and comes to 0 9cm of the lateral  1 4cm of the posterior  0 5cm of the inferior  and 2 2cm of the superior margin  The surrounding focally dense gray white fibrous tissue shows cystic change  The clear serous fluid filled cysts average 0 2cm in diameter  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm gray yellow calcification within the dense gray white fibrous tissue  0 9cm from the cavity and 1 4cm from the closest posterior margin in the mid to inferior portion of the specimen  Another cluster of gritty tan yellow calcifications measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  and is located inferior to the first  0 4cm from the closest medial margin  and 1 7cm from the cavity  The remaining fibrous tissue shows focal nodularity with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the cavity to closest margins as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The first calcified focus is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the second as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections along the posterior and posteromedial aspect of the cavity  the region corresponding to the margin of concern in the prior excision  are submitted from superior to inferior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by John H Eichhorn M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by John H Eichhorn M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  This case was reviewed again  and at the request of the patient  who is a physician  additional tissue from the specimen was submitted for processing in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   A single duct in profile within the biopsy cavity wall on one of the eight additional slides shows residual ductal carcinoma in situ  and this tiny focus is 1 0cm from a blue inked margin  anterior   No stromal or lymphatic invasion is identified in the additional sections  Fibrocystic changes  harboring calcifications  are again noted  Addendum  1 by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT  RE  EXCISION , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 33 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  WITH FOCI SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    LOW GRADE ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT AND WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS   SEE NOTE   3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The margins are free of ductal carcinoma in situ  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST   NEW MARGIN   EXCISION   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 17                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast tissue with short stitch posteriorly  2 pins  long stitch   1 pin  laterally  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm ill defined tan white  firm mass that abuts the lateral margin  Representative section of tumor at the closest  lateral  margin is frozen as FX 1 and the is submitted in cassette A  The extreme posterior margin is submitted in cassette B and the next adjacent section is submitted in cassette C  The posterior margin is double inked with green color and the anterior margin inked black in cassette C   The tumor closest to the closest margin  lateral  is submitted in cassette D  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  new margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibrofatty tissue  Long stitch is in the lateral side and the short stitch in the superior side  The old margin is inked in black and the new lateral margin is inked in blue  The superior margin is inked in red  Representative section taken through the old margin and the new margins are presented in cassettes E G  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                              