was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a left modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a 22 x 21 x 4cm left breast  with a suture designating the superior margin  There is an overlying  20 x 12cm  tan ellipse of skin with an unremarkable nipple areola complex  No gross scars or abnormalities are noted on the skin ellipse  Sectioning through the specimen reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  well delineated  hard  focally gritty  white pink mass located in the lower  inner quadrant  coming within 2 0cm of the deep resection margin  The tumor is located 5 5cm from the inferior margin  9 5cm from the superior margin  4 0cm from the medial margin  and 15cm from the lateral margin  The mass comes within 1 0cm of the nearest skin margin  with no gross involvement of the nipple  The mass is surrounded by a moderate amount of dense  white  fibrous tissue  1 5cm inferomedial to the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  firm nodule  F   The remaining parenchyma is composed predominantly of irregular  white  dense nodules of fibrous tissue with minimal areas of cystification measuring up to 0 5cm in greatest dimension  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm attached axillary tail from which multiple  rubbery lymph nodes are identified  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Section code  A  Tumor in relation to deep margin B C  Tumor 