veal a large excisional cavity  7 0cm in its largest dimension  present 4 0cm from the medial margin  7 0cm from the lateral margin  1 0cm to the superior margin  2 0cm to the inferior margin  and 3 0cm from the deep margin  On the surface of the cavity are several yellow pink nodules  probably consistent with previous biopsy  Further sectioning reveals another REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  yellow pink  firm  rubbery mass present 3 0cm lateral to the biopsy cavity and 9 0cm to the lateral margin  3 0cm to the superior and inferior margins  and 4 0cm to the anterior and deep margins  Representative tissues are submitted in Cassettes A I  Section Code  A B  Superior and lateral wall of excision cavity  C  Anterior side of cavity wall  D  Grossly normal deep medial margin of the cavity  E  Fibrotic mass  F  Fibrotic mass at its deep margin  G  Additional tissues from fibrotic mass  H  Medial margin  I  Lateral margin and one lymph node of REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  present  0 2cm from the lateral margin  K  Two pieces of 2cm lymph nodes Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labelled with the patient s name and unit number and  axillary contents   is an aggregate of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  fatty  lymphoid tissue dissected the identified lymph node submitted in Cassette L  Resident  MANCONG ZHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  OR ROOM UNKNOWN REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT  DISSECTION   report_end  , Absent.
